# IMP — a gaunt, hunched demon that throws fireballs (owner, 2026-10-24: "a
# demonic humanoid that throws fireballs, in the spirit of the Doom 3 imp").
# Pale grey-white leathery hide over a starved frame, a raw wound in the
# chest, long sinewy arms ending in big claws, digitigrade legs, a predatory
# crouch. Quick and agile, not a shambler. The reference is a point
# of departure, not a target (owner): the head's proportions are the twinhead's
# demon skull's, under the hide.
#
# THE CONVERSION (biomech-style.md: "treat every enemy as a strogg
# conversion"). The fire has a source: a skullmetal forge-heart set in the chest
# wound, the fire showing through a slit in it, the broken ribs gripping it, and
# burning fuel lines from it over the ribs and down the arms into the hands. The
# hands are no hands at all but burning SOCKETS caged by fused talons, and the
# fireball leaves from one at the throw (MotionProfile.spit from the hand tip).
# The head is flesh over a simplified demon skull, its eyes burning red.
#
# THE SPLIT: flesh is prims (few: the silhouette); sinew, veins and the
# starved ribs are the baked body normal map (imp.detail); the teeth, horns,
# talons, sockets, the heart, fuel lines, spines and foot claws are kit
# (assets-source/imp-kit/), with thin cores under them.
#
# THE SKELETON is the butcher's (butcher.blob explains the reverse-knee legs
# on the three standard leg bones), hunched deeper, with longer arms and a
# HAND bone so the socket rides its own frame through a throw.
model imp
  height 1.80
  stance humanoid

skeleton
  # Short legs under a long body (owner, 2026-11-02: legs "take up less overall length"): 0.868 m of drop from the
  # hip at 0.90, against the butcher's 1.108 from 1.14. Everything above the hips sits 0.24 lower than the numbers
  # it was designed at (LOWER in imp-detail-gen.ts and imp_common.py).
  root pelvis at 0.76

  # A deep predatory hunch (the reference's crouch): the chest pitched 26 deg
  # forward of the hips (the butcher's 9.8 read upright in profile, first
  # look), the neck thrust out near level and the skull carried low and
  # forward of the chest, not stacked on it.
  bone spine parent=pelvis dir=up pitch=26 len=0.34
  bone neck  parent=spine  dir=up pitch=50 len=0.15
  bone skull parent=neck   dir=up pitch=28 len=0.20

  mirror
    bone clavicle parent=spine    dir=side                     len=0.20
    # LONG ARMS, the hands at the knees: 0.29 + 0.28 + 0.13. (0.34 + 0.33 hung
    # below the knees once the legs were shortened: gangly.) Held out (tilt 20) and
    # forward (pitch 14, then 30 on the forearm): the claws lead, the way a
    # stalking imp carries them, and they clear the thighs in the crouch.
    bone upperArm parent=clavicle dir=down tilt=20 pitch=14    len=0.29
    bone foreArm  parent=upperArm dir=down tilt=6 pitch=30     len=0.28
    bone hand     parent=foreArm  dir=down pitch=40            len=0.13
    # THE LEG: the butcher's angles (butcher.blob) on shorter bones (his 0.40, 0.50, 0.40), the metatarsal cut most,
    # so the big foot on the floor is the read.
    bone thigh    parent=pelvis   dir=down side=0.13 pitch=35  len=0.33
    bone shin     parent=thigh    dir=down pitch=-38           len=0.40
    bone foot     parent=shin     dir=down pitch=15            len=0.293
  end

body
  # Neck: stringy and long, thrust forward out of the hunch.
  bar head on neck from=0.0 to=1.0 r=0.052 r2=0.048 blend=0.012

  # HEAD — flesh over a simplified DEMON SKULL: the twinhead kit's skull
  # (assets-source/twinhead-kit, skull|demonskull) as the armature under the
  # hide (owner, 2026-10-24: "the proportions as a starting point ... a
  # simplified version of the skull under the SDF flesh"). Its read, in prims:
  # a long domed cranium, a heavy brow ridge in a V, sunken slanted sockets with
  # red eyes, cheekbones flaring back to the temples, a long narrow muzzle and a
  # hard jaw with a chin point. Teeth and the swept-back horns are kit.
  # Offsets are world axes at rest from the skull bone at 0.30. The whole head is 1.25x its first size (owner,
  # 2026-11-02: "head bigger"), the kit's teeth and horns with it (make_head.py HS).
  # Cranium: long and low, swept back over the neck.
  # Narrower than the brows and blended wide, so it tapers into the temples:
  # at wide 0.90 its equator overhung the face like a cap's brim.
  blob head on skull at=0.30 offset=(0,0.0725,-0.0438) r=0.1063 wide=0.78 tall=0.88 deep=1.28 blend=0.0325
  # The nape: where the neck swells into the skull's base, the head's CORE (the
  # validator fuses clusters along the straight line between cores; from the
  # cranium's centre that line left the hunched neck).
  blob head on skull at=0.00 offset=(0,0.015,-0.0125) r=0.0575 blend=0.0175 core
  # Brow ridges: one per side in a V (the skull's scowl), low at the bridge and
  # rising to the temple, overhanging the sockets. One bar straight across read
  # as a hat brim.
  # Kept inside the temples: run out to x 0.058 the pair read as a hat brim.
  bar  head on skull from=0.30 to=0.30 offset=(0.0075,0.0775,0.12) tip=(0.045,0.0175,-0.0325) bend=(0,0.0025,0.005) r=0.0137 tall=0.80 blend=0.0125 both
  # Cheekbones: flaring wide below the sockets and sweeping back to the temples.
  bar  head on skull from=0.30 to=0.30 offset=(0.045,0.0375,0.0975) tip=(0.03,0.0125,-0.0875) r=0.0213 r2=0.015 blend=0.0125 both
  # The muzzle: a long narrow maxilla thrust forward, the skull's snout.
  blob head on skull at=0.30 offset=(0,0.01,0.1225) r=0.05 wide=0.86 tall=0.72 deep=1.40 blend=0.015
  # FLARED NOSTRILS (owner: "flared nostrils or something"): two swollen alae
  # on top of the muzzle's front, splayed out and back, each with a dark slit
  # raking up and out (the skull's nasal cavity, under the hide).
  # Narrow slits raked up the muzzle, not holes facing front: round dark holes
  # a centimetre across read as a pig's snout (biomech-style.md's warning).
  blob head on skull at=0.30 offset=(0.0225,0.0325,0.15) r=0.0106 wide=1.10 tall=0.80 deep=1.20 blend=0.0088 both
  bar  head on skull from=0.30 to=0.30 offset=(0.01,0.0325,0.17) tip=(0.0137,0.01,-0.0175) r=0.0032 deep=0.7 blend=0.0019 both color=1c0707 gloss=0.6
  # The jaw: two mandible bars from the angle to a hard chin point.
  bar  head on skull from=0.30 to=0.30 offset=(0.05,-0.0125,0.005) tip=(-0.0475,-0.04,0.1325) r=0.0225 r2=0.0163 blend=0.0125 both
  # Thrust forward to the mouth slot's front, so the lower teeth stand on it.
  blob head on skull at=0.30 offset=(0,-0.0575,0.15) r=0.0275 wide=1.10 tall=0.90 deep=1.00 blend=0.0125
  # Sockets: sunken dark hollows under the brow, slanted (outer end higher),
  # with a bridge of flesh between them (from 0.016 they met in the middle and
  # read as one goggle band), each with a small red ember sunk in it (the
  # skull's burning eyes; owner: red).
  bar  head on skull from=0.30 to=0.30 offset=(0.0263,0.0625,0.1125) tip=(0.0275,0.0125,-0.0175) r=0.0131 tall=0.80 deep=0.55 blend=0.005 both color=1c0707 gloss=0.3
  blob head on skull at=0.30 offset=(0.0387,0.0688,0.11) r=0.0069 blend=0.0025 both color=ff2410 glow=0.9
  # The mouth: a dark slot between muzzle and jaw, the kit teeth set on its edges.
  # (At wide 1.55 it stood out past the jaw's sides and read as a black collar.)
  # A gape, not a line: tall enough that the teeth (kit, rooted in the flesh
  # above and below it) stand against the dark.
  blob head on skull at=0.30 offset=(0,-0.0225,0.16) r=0.035 wide=1.15 tall=0.80 deep=0.50 blend=0.0037 color=2a0a0c gloss=0.9

  # TORSO — the flayer's gaunt masses (flayer.blob), the chest narrower and
  # the waist pinched: starved, every rib in the normal map.
  blob torso on spine  at=0.80 r=0.150 wide=1.36 deep=0.78 blend=0.016
  blob torso on spine  at=0.50 r=0.136 wide=1.12 deep=0.80 blend=0.02
  blob torso on spine  at=0.15 r=0.112 wide=1.00 deep=0.88 blend=0.02
  # The yoke: wiry traps and the shoulder girdle the long arms hang from, so
  # the upper body reads broad over the starved waist (first look: a narrow
  # mannequin with arms on a coat hanger).
  blob torso on spine  at=0.98 offset=(0.09,-0.01,-0.02) r=0.075 wide=1.25 tall=0.80 deep=0.95 blend=0.022 both
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.40 r=0.125 wide=1.04 tall=0.9 deep=0.90 blend=0.02
  # The CHEST WOUND: raw meat proud of the sternum where the forge-heart (kit)
  # sits in it, and the dark socket inside it. Muted red (the
  # teratoma's lesson: hex reds render hotter than they read). Blended wide and
  # flat, so it melts into the hide: at blend 0.006 its hard rim read as a saucer.
  blob torso on spine  at=0.62 offset=(0,0,0.088) r=0.062 wide=1.20 tall=1.25 deep=0.45 blend=0.018 color=7a3c3c gloss=0.85
  blob torso on spine  at=0.62 offset=(0,0,0.118) r=0.036 wide=1.10 tall=1.30 deep=0.50 blend=0.004 color=2a0a0c gloss=0.9

  # ARMS — long and stringy: thin upper arms, the forearm swelling below the
  # elbow (the sinew is in the normal map), the hand a thin core inside the
  # kit's talons and socket.
  # Deltoid: a bony knob of a shoulder, wider than the arm below it.
  blob arm on clavicle at=0.95 r=0.070 wide=1.10 blend=0.012 mirror
  bar  arm on upperArm from=0.02 to=0.96 r=0.046 r2=0.036 blend=0.008 mirror
  bar  arm on foreArm  from=0.04 to=0.95 r=0.050 r2=0.032 blend=0.008 mirror
  # The forearm's belly, just below the elbow: the sinewy swell of the
  # reference, fatter than the upper arm (the tubes read uniform, first look).
  blob arm on foreArm  at=0.30 offset=(0,0,-0.006) r=0.052 tall=2.0 blend=0.012 mirror
  blob arm on hand     at=0.30 r=0.034 wide=1.15 deep=0.85 blend=0.008 mirror

  # LEGS — flesh, digitigrade: a lean haunch, a thin thigh, a ropy shin to the
  # hock and a long bony metatarsal. The claws at the toes are kit.
  # The haunch, seated down the femur: at r 0.088 on the hip joint it swelled
  # behind like buttocks in profile (first look).
  blob leg on thigh at=0.20 r=0.082 blend=0.018 mirror
  # A runner's thigh, a little deeper than wide. The owner on a thinner pass
  # (r 0.060, wide 0.80): "his thighs and legs are a bit too skinny".
  bar  leg on thigh from=0.06 to=0.96 r=0.074 r2=0.050 wide=0.92 blend=0.012 mirror
  bar  leg on shin  from=0.02 to=0.96 r=0.060 r2=0.042 blend=0.010 mirror
  # The calf belly on the BACK of the tibia's upper half (the digitigrade
  # shin's gastrocnemius), so the lower leg tapers to a ropy tendon at the hock.
  blob leg on shin  at=0.30 offset=(0,0,-0.022) r=0.058 tall=1.9 blend=0.016 mirror
  # The metatarsal: still the leg's thinnest run, but not a stick (at r 0.030
  # it read as a stilt from the front).
  bar  leg on foot  from=0.02 to=0.98 r=0.046 r2=0.042 blend=0.010 mirror
  # BIG SPLAYED CLAW FEET (owner, 2026-11-02, with a reference: "big splaying claw type feet"): meat, not a pad with
  # talons on it. A broad ball of the foot, three long thick toes fanned wide along the floor, each arched over a
  # knuckle, and a short back toe. The claws are kit, on these tips (make_feet.py TOES repeats the numbers).
  # Thick: at r 0.033 -> 0.020 they read as a bird's foot.
  blob leg on foot  at=1.00 offset=(0,0.022,0.040) r=0.074 wide=1.35 tall=0.62 deep=1.20 blend=0.016 mirror
  bar  leg on foot  from=1.00 to=1.00 offset=(0,0.026,0.060) tip=(0,-0.026,0.200) bend=(0,0.040,0) r=0.046 r2=0.030 blend=0.012 mirror
  blob leg on foot  at=1.00 offset=(0,0.045,0.150) r=0.044 wide=1.05 tall=0.85 deep=1.20 blend=0.010 mirror
  bar  leg on foot  from=1.00 to=1.00 offset=(0.045,0.024,0.045) tip=(0.105,-0.024,0.155) bend=(0,0.036,0) r=0.042 r2=0.028 blend=0.012 mirror
  blob leg on foot  at=1.00 offset=(0.090,0.040,0.120) r=0.040 wide=1.05 tall=0.85 deep=1.20 blend=0.010 mirror
  bar  leg on foot  from=1.00 to=1.00 offset=(-0.040,0.024,0.045) tip=(-0.040,-0.024,0.145) bend=(0,0.034,0) r=0.041 r2=0.028 blend=0.012 mirror
  blob leg on foot  at=1.00 offset=(-0.058,0.038,0.112) r=0.039 wide=1.05 tall=0.85 deep=1.20 blend=0.010 mirror
  bar  leg on foot  from=1.00 to=1.00 offset=(0,0.024,-0.005) tip=(0,-0.024,-0.100) bend=(0,0.018,0) r=0.034 r2=0.024 blend=0.012 mirror

bones
  ratio 0.38
  # THE HEAD'S BONE is the demon skull itself (owner, 2026-11-02: shot open, the head showed "the simplified humanoid
  # skull", a ball with a face painted on): the flesh head's skull lines above, cranium, nape, V brows, cheekbones,
  # muzzle, jaw and chin, at 0.85 round the same points so it sits under the hide; the sockets, nostrils and mouth are
  # flesh colour, not bone. Regenerate from the HEAD lines if they change.
  blob head on skull at=0.30 offset=(0,0.0648,-0.0323) r=0.0797 wide=0.78 tall=0.88 deep=1.28 blend=0.0244
  blob head on skull at=0.00 offset=(0,0.0123,-0.0103) r=0.0431 blend=0.0131
  bar  head on skull from=0.30 to=0.30 offset=(0.0369,0.0362,0.0835) tip=(0.0246,0.0103,-0.0717) r=0.016 r2=0.0112 blend=0.0094 both
  blob head on skull at=0.30 offset=(0,0.0136,0.104) r=0.0375 wide=0.86 tall=0.72 deep=1.40 blend=0.0112
  blob head on skull at=0.30 offset=(0.0184,0.0321,0.1266) r=0.008 wide=1.10 tall=0.80 deep=1.20 blend=0.0066 both
  blob head on skull at=0.30 offset=(0,-0.0417,0.1266) r=0.0165 wide=1.10 tall=0.90 deep=1.00 blend=0.0094
  # The brows and mandibles, re-cut for the bone (the flesh's own lines breached the hide at the bridge, the temples
  # and the lip: the hide over them is thin): the brow higher and shorter, the jaw stopping short of the chin.
  bar  head on skull from=0.30 to=0.30 offset=(0.014,0.078,0.062) tip=(0.022,0.010,-0.030) r=0.012 tall=0.8 blend=0.008 both
  bar  head on skull from=0.30 to=0.30 offset=(0.040,-0.016,0.020) tip=(-0.026,-0.022,0.072) r=0.013 r2=0.010 blend=0.008 both
  # The zombie's spinal column is left out: under this hunch and the pinched
  # starved waist it breached the back at both the kyphosis (y 1.23) and the
  # lumbar curve (y 1.17). The spine ridge is the normal map's.

# No generated face: the head is prims and kit (twinhead's blanking block).
face
  headRadius 0.001
  headWidth  1.0
  headHeight 1.0
  headDepth  1.0
  jawWidth   1.0
  jawHeight  1.0
  jawDrop    0
  jawJut     0
  noseLength 0
  noseWidth  1.0
  noseDrop   0
  browHeavy  0
  browRise   0
  headBlend  0.006

# Pale grey-white leather: a cool grey, barely pink, a dry sheen rather than
# the zombie's wet flesh, mottled with a dirty grey-brown. Low translucency
# (hide, not skin).
palette
  baseColor     0.66 0.64 0.62
  deepColor     0.50 0.07 0.07
  charColor     0.08 0.07 0.07
  specIntensity 0.65
  specRoughness 0.30
  fresnelBoost  0.55
  translucency  0.18
  wetness       0.35
  surfaceNoiseAmp    0.030
  silhouetteNoiseAmp 0.010
  mottleAmp     0.45
  mottleScale   2.4
  mottleColor   0.40 0.37 0.34
  # Low: at 0.10 the hide read as a pixel checker up close.
  grain         0.04

sheet
  # NO FACE SHEET: the face is prims and kit (the gorehound's lesson: a sheet
  # left on lands on whatever flesh sits at the head's front).
  enabled 0
